# Machine-specific i3 config (not tracked in dotfiles).
#
# The main config does `include ~/.config/i3/local.conf` at the end, so anything
# here is layered on top per machine. install.sh seeds this file from
# local.conf.example only if it does not already exist, so your edits are safe.
#
# Typical use: monitor layout and per-output workspace assignments. These are
# inherently machine-specific (different displays, different names), so the
# examples below are commented out — uncomment and adapt to the machine.

# --- Monitor setup ---
# Point this at a machine-local ~/.local/bin/setup-monitors.sh that runs the
# right xrandr command for this machine's displays. Runs once at i3 startup.
# exec --no-startup-id setup-monitors.sh

# --- Workspace output assignments ---
# Pin specific workspaces to a specific output (find names with `xrandr`).
# workspace 7 output DP-4
# workspace 8 output DP-4
# workspace 9 output DP-4
# workspace 10 output DP-4
